Description: Disable Google Storage downloads for network isolation
 For Debian builds, all required source files must be present in the source
 tarball. This patch disables download_from_google_storage.py to enforce
 network isolation during package builds.
 .
 The script is called by gclient hooks to download test data files from
 Google Cloud Storage (gs://chromium-telemetry/). In Debian builds, these
 downloads are forbidden by policy.
 .
 This patch makes the script a no-op by returning immediately. Any missing
 test data will be caught during build, not silently downloaded.
 .
 Impact: Enforces Debian network isolation policy, prevents silent downloads
 during build, ensures all build artifacts come from source tarball only.
Author: Juan Manuel Méndez Rey <juan.mendezr@proton.me>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2025-11-10

--- a/download_from_google_storage.py
+++ b/download_from_google_storage.py
@@ -565,6 +565,10 @@ def download_from_google_storage(

 def main(args):
+    # Debian: Network isolation - disable all Google Storage downloads
+    # All required files must be present in source tarball
+    return 0
+
     usage = ('usage: %prog [options] target\n'
              'Target must be:\n'
              '  (default) a sha1 sum ([A-Za-z0-9]{40}).\n'
